From 2ef3da4a19db91b63e5036773a4b569a72b4a8e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Helldez <74499579+Helldez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Apr 2026 09:48:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(parakeet,sdk): mid-segment partial decoding for live
 streaming

Adds a partial-decode loop to the parakeet streaming addon for live
dictation UX and propagates the resulting isPartial flag end-to-end
through the SDK's transcribeStream duplex API.

qvac-lib-infer-parakeet (native):
- StreamingProcessor.Config.partialDecodeIntervalSamples (default 1.5 s).
- While Silero reports an open segment, processLoop re-runs the recognizer
  on the live range every N samples of new audio and queues the output
  with isPartial=true. Skipped on the same iteration that trims a final
  segment, since the segments[] timestamps are then stale.
- ParakeetTypes.Transcript gains isPartial; AddonJs.startStreaming reads
  partialDecodeIntervalMs from the JS config; AddonJs output handler
  serializes isPartial onto each emitted JS object.
- index.js / index.d.ts forward partial_decode_interval_ms from
  vad_params into the addon.

sdk:
- transcribeStreamResponseSchema.isPartial?: boolean.
- vadParamsSchema.partial_decode_interval_ms?: number.
- bare ops/transcribe.ts yields {text, isPartial}; parakeet plugin
  handler propagates it into the duplex frame.
- Client transcribe.ts parseResponseLines yields {text, isPartial} and
  TranscribeStreamSession's iterator type follows.

The recognizer's behavior is otherwise unchanged: callers that don't set
partial_decode_interval_ms get the legacy final-only stream.
